WEBVTT

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:09.170
I'll let you guys go unharmed
as long as you cooperate.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.950
What's this?

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.740
You have a minute left! Hurry!

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.590
What's the matter?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.930
<i>Bank robbery in progress at F District</i>
<i>Capital Bank. Requesting backup.</i>

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.530
It was me.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.160
Big mistake.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.350
Forget her! Let's go!

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.640
Come on.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.230
Damn it.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.750
Damn it. Hurry up already.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.180
Hey!

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.350
Damn it.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.790
The ambulance is coming.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.390
<i>Richard.</i>

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.800
Olivia! Are you okay?

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.020
Yes, I'm okay.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.480
<i>Thank God.</i>

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:19.730
I...

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.280
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.360
I'm on my way now. I'll be there soon.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.160
I love you.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.250
I know.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.470
Richard.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.100
What is it?

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.360
Come on, what?

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.730
I'll be there soon.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.860
Richard...

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:12.700
happy anniversary--

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.430
Who are you?

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.900
Tell me who gave you the orders.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:09.030
Are you... a cop?

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.280
I didn't know anything!

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.740
Everything was done over the phone.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.740
And I met the crew that day
for the first time.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.580
I wouldn't have taken the job if I knew
they were going to kill me!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.130
I didn't know they had set bombs!

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.170
I was almost killed!

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:37.300
They'll come and kill me
once they find out that I'm alive.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.430
Look, I'm a witness.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.190
Isn't it part of your job
to protect witnesses, too?

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.360
So, put the gun down and protect me.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.900
If you think about it, I'm a victim, too,
you know?

00:08:58.370 --> 00:08:59.370
Stop! Don't!

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.120
That's enough!

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:35.280
It's about the body they found
in the river the other day.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:41.660
There are a few things
I found interesting.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:48.370
First, it's highly likely
that he was murdered.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.710
And second, he was an owner
of a safety-deposit box.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.470
It belonged to the bank that was attacked.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:03.180
He had been keeping something
in that bank.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.060
The murder victim was an accountant
for LIVE Corporation.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.520
It's a corporation that grew explosively

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:14.650
by continually announcing
mergers and acquisitions.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:22.530
According to testimony, the sole target
for this robbery was a single notebook.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.870
It's possible that this accountant
happened to have discovered some secret

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.750
and had been writing in the notebook.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:43.950
<i>New allegations emerge against</i>
<i>LIVE Corporation chairman,</i>

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:47.120
<i>Steven Martland, who is already</i>
<i>under suspicion for bribery.</i>

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:51.120
<i>LIVE Corporation appears to have been</i>
<i>a part of an illegal arms ring.</i>

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.170
<i>Martland denies all charges.</i>

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:59.050
<i>The weapons were traded</i>
<i>to both sides in areas of conflict.</i>

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:03.430
<i>Experts say this caused tensions</i>
<i>to escalate, prolonging the conflict.</i>

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.640
<i>After being taken into custody,</i>

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.010
<i>Martland cooperated</i>
<i>with police questioning</i>

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.970
<i>and is scheduled to be released on bail.</i>

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.020
<i>This was a big blow</i>
<i>to LIVE Corporation's efforts</i>

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.690
<i>in expanding</i>
<i>their humanitarian aid programs.</i>

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.650
It's not looking good.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.530
Apparently.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:29.740
The blood you've spilled
must be paid with your own blood.

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.140
In the past...

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.770
there was a bank bombing in this city
that took many lives.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.060
What about it?

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.020
My wife was one of the victims.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.740
Well, you have my condolences.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:10.120
But we're all subject
to the unpredictability of life.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:14.160
Who knew I'd end up becoming a suspect.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.710
Are you saying
you weren't anticipating this?

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:22.420
The Mask has certainly
thrown a wrench in my plans,

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:25.880
but it's the uncertainty like this
that I enjoy.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:33.600
Nothing shall disturb my game, whatsoever.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:39.270
It is I who continues to control the game.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.770
Even if you change faces?

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:56.500
In this world, there are excellent
detectives and capable detectives.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.170
You seem to be the former.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:06.170
However, excellent detectives
tend to live shorter lives.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:13.930
Good day.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:29.450
Could we get a statement
regarding this arrest?

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:30.950
Please, sir!

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:35.160
I strongly object to the police conducting
a one-sided investigation

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.500
and pushing biased evidence.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.830
Then you wish to deny these charges
once again?

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.290
The charges are baseless.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:49.840
I am confident that further investigation
will completely exonerate me.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.930
What do you mean?

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:55.220
-What will happen with LIVE?
-Please answer!

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.690
Martland seems to be heading
to the hospital.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:34.970
Pull over.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:47.820
I'd like to stretch my legs.
Will you excuse me.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.210
Eddy is searching, too,
but it's proving difficult.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.090
Look into companies connected to LIVE,
his home, the hospital...

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.510
I mean everything.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.400
Mr. Steven Martland...

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:12.110
thanks for all the good memories.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:56.400
Now, let the new game begin.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.670
<i>Mr. Martland disappeared</i>
<i>shortly after being released on bail.</i>

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.970
<i>He has not yet been found</i>
<i>after a day of search.</i>

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.800
<i>Taking this into account,</i>
<i>it is likely that prosecutors</i>

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:22.970
<i>will revisit past investigations</i>
<i>against LIVE Corporation.</i>

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.050
That's so cute.

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:10.060
-Go back! I want to see it again.
-This right here.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.100
It's so cute!

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.810
Hey, have you seen this?

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:16.350
Nope.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.030
-Let me see it again.
-Here.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.240
Make it bigger.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.660
It's so cute!

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:21.870
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
